  "chapter": {
    "number": 87,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(88) A song of a Psalm for the sons of Core for the end, upon Maeleth for responsive strains, of",
          {
            "noteId": 157
          },
          "instruction for Aeman the Israelite."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord God of my salvation, I have cried by day and in the night before you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let my prayer come in before you; incline your ear to my supplication, O Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For my soul is filled with troubles, and my life has drawn near to Hades.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I have been reckoned with them that go down to the pit; I became as a man without help;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "free among the dead, as the slain ones",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 158
          },
          {
            "text": "cast out, who sleep in the tomb; whom you remember no more; and they are rejected from your hand.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They laid me in the lowest pit, in dark places, and in the shadow of death.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Your wrath has pressed heavily upon me, and you have brought upon me all your billows. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have removed my acquaintance far from me; they have made me an abomination to themselves; I have been delivered up, and have not gone forth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My eyes are dimmed from poverty; but I cried to you, O Lord, all the day; I spread forth my hands to you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Will you work wonders for the dead? or shall",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 159
          },
          {
            "text": "physicians raise them up, that they shall praise you?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Shall any one declare your mercy in the tomb? and your truth in destruction?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Shall your wonders be known in darkness? and your righteousness in a forgotten land?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But I cried to you, O Lord; and in the morning shall my prayer prevent you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Therefore, O Lord, do you reject my",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 160
          },
          {
            "text": "prayer, and turn your face away from me?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I am poor and in troubles from my youth; and having been exalted, I was brought low and into",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 161
          },
          {
            "text": "despair.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Your wrath has passed over me; and your terrors have greatly disquieted me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They compassed me like water; all the day they beset me together.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have put far from me",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 162
          },
          {
            "text": "every friend, and my acquaintances because of my wretchedness.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
